		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T21:26:40Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Use username in dev PostHog identifier fallback\n\nThe previous implementation used `Date.now()` in the PostHog identifier fallback, generating a different random seed for every editor launch. This made it difficult to correlate telemetry events from the same development machine across sessions.\n\nUpdate the fallback logic to extract the username from `USER` or `USERNAME` environment variables, producing a stable `land-dev-wind-{Username}` identifier that persists across editor restarts.\n\nThis improves debuggability of development telemetry by allowing filtering by machine/username.",
			"SHA": "de951d2eb5e19263f4251bb6262c6aa65d32f0d7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T20:52:32Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1049,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Wind): Add missing IPC stub channels for webview, watcher, urlHandler, and download services\n\nAdd four new stub channel definitions to TauriMainProcessService's StubChannels to prevent \"Unknown method\" errors during workbench boot:\n\n- `webview`: IWebviewManagerService stub - disables native menu shortcuts in electron but is no-op in Tauri's WKWebView\n- `watcher`: IFileWatcherService stub - Land routes file watching via Mountain's FileWatcher.Register IPC instead\n- `urlHandler`: IURLService stub - vscode:// URI handlers register through this; stub to no-ops for extensions calling registerUriHandler\n- `download`: IDownloadService stub - extension gallery download path; returns undefined to surface \"download not supported\"\n\nThese stubs mirror the Output copy to maintain the Wind/Output lockstep rule. Without them, extensions or workbench services calling these channels hit undefined method paths during initialization.",
			"SHA": "40b3c5c946f0b4256c0fe5c220b7187749c62725"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T03:23:03Z",
